 "scope": "",
 "statement": "Three scalar-field Lean endpoints reuse pinned existing Mathlib/CryptoLean laws: kernel cancellation under checked matrix/vector and nonzero-tag contracts; exact mixed-label fiber cardinality; and exact nonzero-functional annihilator cardinality times ell equals ell^r. Scalar modulus is the standard Curve25519 ell, under an explicit primality hypothesis. Producer gate passes with only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound, no native exception. Full curve-group, retained-row uniformity/selection, geometry and decomposition-cost bridges are outside these theorem statements; no attack exponent or unknown DLP solve is proved."
